@startuml autonomous-offering-concept
title Autonomous Offering Concept ; per ADR-ES-019 + CR-ES-019

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

abstract class "Offering" as O {
  +offering_intent
  +offering_value
}

class "Autonomous Offering" as AO {
  +offering_objective
  +autonomy_scope
  +offering_context
  +decision_scope
  +action_scope
  +configuration_scope
  +composition_scope
  +coordination_scope
  +authority_context
  +policy_context
  +constraint_context
  +governance_context
  +adaptation_scope
  +intervention_model
  +escalation_boundary
  +observation_scope
  +realization_mode
}

O <|-- AO : specializes

class "Authority" as Auth
class "Policy" as Pol
class "Constraint" as Con
class "Governance" as Gov
class "Objective" as Obj
class "Outcome" as Out
class "Context" as Ctx
class "Escalation" as Esc
class "Autonomous Product" as AP
class "Autonomous Service" as AS
class "Agentic Workflow" as AW

AO --> Auth : operates-within
AO --> Pol : governed-by
AO --> Con : constrained-by
AO --> Gov : operates-within
AO --> Obj : pursues
AO --> Ctx : responds-to
AO --> Out : produces
AO --> Ctx : adapts-to
AO --> Esc : escalates-to
AO --> AP : uses
AO --> AS : uses
AO --> AW : uses

note right of AO
  Autonomous Materiality required per ADR-ES-019 section 6.
  AI NOT required per ADR-ES-019 section 14.
  Automation NOT sufficient per ADR-ES-019 section 15.
  Human participation remains valid per ADR-ES-019 section 7.
  Bounded by 6 fences: Objective -> Authority -> Policy -> Constraints -> Governance -> Escalation.
  Foundational Dependency Gate documented per ADR-ES-019 section 2.
end note

@enduml
